/* Uruk Academy — Biology Ch.1 «الخلية» (The Cell).
   Scope follows the verified structure in research/biology-structure.md
   §2-Ch.1 (sections 1-1…7-1 of the ministry book): cell theory and its
   founders, cell size and surface area, the prokaryotic cell, the
   eukaryotic cell and all its organelles, cellular activities (transport
   across membranes, endocytosis and exocytosis, metabolism, aerobic and
   anaerobic respiration, nucleic acids in general composition), and cell
   division (mitosis with its four phases, cytokinesis and the plant cell
   plate, meiosis with its two divisions). Respiration accounting follows
   the authoring spec: the anaerobic net yield is stated as the hard
   number 2 ATP from glycolysis only; the aerobic yield is compared
   qualitatively as much larger, with no undocumented total.
   All explanations, examples and questions are original and were
   re-derived at authoring time. */

